Welcome to WindClone.

This text is not compiled into the kernel. The bootloader loaded
it as a module (a plain ustar tar archive), and the kernel parsed
that archive in place and read this file out of it.

That is the whole point of an initrd: userland data the kernel does
not have to be rebuilt to change. Phase 4 grows this into a real
filesystem, an ELF loader and the first ring-3 process.
